  "title": "Job 4",
  "display_title": "Job 4",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 4,
  "sortOrder": 18004,
  "verseCount": 21,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "If we assay to commune with thee, wilt thou be grieved? but who can withhold himself from speaking?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Behold, thou hast instructed many, and thou hast strengthened the weak hands.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Thy words have upholden him that was falling, and thou hast strengthened the feeble knees.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "But now it is come upon thee, and thou faintest; it toucheth thee, and thou art troubled.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Is not this thy fear, thy confidence, thy hope, and the uprightness of thy ways?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Remember, I pray thee, who ever perished, being innocent? or where were the righteous cut off?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Even as I have seen, they that plow iniquity, and sow wickedness, reap the same.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "By the blast of God they perish, and by the breath of his nostrils are they consumed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "The roaring of the lion, and the voice of the fierce lion, and the teeth of the young lions, are broken.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "The old lion perisheth for lack of prey, and the stout lion’s whelps are scattered abroad.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Now a thing was secretly brought to me, and mine ear received a little thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "In thoughts from the visions of the night, when deep sleep falleth on men,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Fear came upon me, and trembling, which made all my bones to shake.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Then a spirit passed before my face; the hair of my flesh stood up:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "It stood still, but I could not discern the form thereof: an image was before mine eyes, there was silence, and I heard a voice, saying,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Shall mortal man be more just than God? shall a man be more pure than his maker?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Behold, he put no trust in his servants; and his angels he charged with folly:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "How much less in them that dwell in houses of clay, whose foundation is in the dust, which are crushed before the moth?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "They are destroyed from morning to evening: they perish for ever without any regarding it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:4:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Doth not their excellency which is in them go away? they die, even without wisdom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 4:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:4:21"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
